course: dictionary
lesson: 11478
title: Being part of a bigger group
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Affiliated means officially connected to a bigger group or organisation. Think of a small school that is part of an official family of schools, with proper links to it.
explain: «Our school is affiliated with a famous university.» The word tells you the school has an official link to the university, not just a friendly one. Clue words like «with» and «to» often come right after it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «Our school is officially connected with a famous university.» If that still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Affiliated is an adjective, as in «an affiliated club».
fact: Affiliate is a verb meaning to join or link up with a larger group.
fact: Affiliated is also the past form of affiliate, as in «The club affiliated last year».
fact: Common phrases are affiliated with and affiliated to, as in «affiliated to the national league».
fact: Affiliated is a formal word, so you will often meet it in official letters, websites and notices.
exercise: «The chess club is affiliated to the national league.» What does affiliated mean here? | Closed for the summer | Very tired after a long game | Painted in bright colours | *Officially connected to a bigger group
exercise: What does it mean to affiliate with a group? | To leave a group for ever | To dance in a circle | To count the members | *To join or link up with a larger group
exercise: «We joined an affiliated club.» What kind of word is affiliated here? | A full stop or comma | A noun, a name for a thing | A verb, an action word | *An adjective, describing the club
test: «The hospital is affiliated with the medical college.» What does this tell us about the hospital? | *Officially connected to the medical college | Next door to a park | Made of glass | Closed on Sundays
test: Dani says affiliated is just a fancy word for friends. What is the better answer? | It means friends who play together | *It means officially connected, not just friendly | It means a kind of dog | It means the same as lonely
exam: «The club, affiliated to the national league, has forty members.» Which word shows the club is officially linked to a bigger group? | *affiliated | club | members | forty
